Changelog
=========

Unreleased

- Fixes
  - Declare missing dependencies (pyyaml, defusedxml, numpy) - a clean pip install could not start
  - docx export without template failed on setuptools >= 81 (pkg_resources removed)
  - Crash on non numeric ports such as `package` (local security checks)
  - Excel by-host export crashed on IPv6 hosts (invalid sheet name)
  - CSV by vulnerability: references were split character by character
  - YAML config: regex `includes` were dropped when no `excludes` were given
  - Invalid network filter raised NameError; invalid input files are now reported cleanly
  - Input patterns matching no file are an error instead of an empty report
  - CVSS 0.0 findings were reported as "No CVSS"
  - Installed version extraction captured the rest of the line
  - Excel row heights applied to the wrong rows
  - Parser tolerates missing hostname / severity / tags and tags without '='
  - CLI errors are printed without Python traceback (exit code 1)
  - CSV files are written as UTF-8
  - docx charts no longer touch matplotlib's global state; docx with an empty selection no longer fails
  - A vulnerability found with different severities (overrides, several reports) takes its worst severity
  - Host reports: one row per port even when the same port has several results
  - Existing input paths containing `[]*?` are used as is; `-i` requires at least one file
  - Network filters: host names never match a network (instead of crashing), blank lines are ignored
  - `general/CPE-T` ports keep their full name; results without `<nvt>`/`<host>` are skipped
  - Host reports lost all but one port of a vulnerability found on many ports (issue #49)
- Security
  - XML input with a DTD is refused (memory exhaustion through attribute defaults)
- Tests
  - Integration test suite (`pytest`), run by GitHub Actions on pushes and pull requests

1.6.1

- Fix PyPi upload

1.6.0

- New Features
  - Add Vulnerability version to report
- Fixes
  - Refactor code to help future developpement
  - Class, function and variable are now typed
  - Remove useless part of the script that where not used
  - Bump minimum Python to version 3.12

1.5.0

- Added args options to personnalize IP and CVE to keep/ignore

1.4.2

- Fixed `ValueError: Unknown format code 'f' for object of type 'str'`

1.4.1

- Small bugfixes and code refactoring

1.4.0

- Use Word template for report building

1.3.1

- Add charts to Word document using matplotlib
- Some code clean-up and small lay-out changes in Excel

1.3.0

- Fix retrieval of description and other useful info by parsing `<tags>` instead of `<description>`

1.2.3

- Implement [https://github.com/cr0hn/openvas_to_report/pull/12]

1.2.2

- Fix bug where port info was not correctly extracted

1.2.1

- Fix bug where affected hosts were added on wrong row in Excel export

1.2.0

- Functional export to Word document (.docx)
- Includes some formatting
- TODO: graphs

1.1.0a

- Support for exporting to Word document (.docx)
- Limited formatting, needs more testing

1.0.1a

- Small updates, preparing for export to other formats

1.0.0

- First official release, supports export to Excel with graphs, ToC and worksheet per vulnerability
